  "guideXiaomi": "1. Open Settings > Apps > Manage apps > B4Due.\n2. Turn on \"Autostart\".\n3. Tap \"Battery saver\" and choose \"No restrictions\".\n4. In recent apps, long-press the B4Due card and tap the lock icon.",
  "guideOppo": "1. Open Settings > Apps > App management > B4Due.\n2. Tap \"Battery usage\" and turn on \"Allow background activity\" and \"Allow auto launch\".\n3. In recent apps, open the B4Due card menu and choose \"Lock\".",
  "guideVivo": "1. Open Settings > Battery > High background power consumption and turn on B4Due.\n2. Open Settings > Apps > Autostart and turn on B4Due.\n3. In recent apps, pull the B4Due card down to lock it.",
  "guideSamsung": "1. Open Settings > Apps > B4Due > Battery and choose \"Unrestricted\".\n2. Open Settings > Battery > Background usage limits and make sure B4Due is not in \"Sleeping apps\" or \"Deep sleeping apps\".",
  "guideTranssion": "1. Open Settings > Apps > B4Due > Battery and choose \"No restrictions\".\n2. Open Phone Master > Auto-start and turn on B4Due.\n3. Lock the B4Due card in recent apps.",
  "guideHuawei": "1. Open Settings > Battery > App launch > B4Due.\n2. Turn off \"Manage automatically\" and enable all three options (auto-launch, secondary launch, run in background).",
  "guideOther": "1. Open Settings > Apps > B4Due > Battery.\n2. Choose \"Unrestricted\" or \"Not optimized\".\n3. Make sure B4Due notifications are allowed.",
  "onboardingBatteryTitle": "Don't let your phone close B4Due",
  "onboardingBatteryBody": "Battery savers on many phones can delay reminders. Let B4Due run in the background. The app is very light on battery.",
